/* =====================================================================================
   DM-A2  |  Attribute Checks - Record-level Attribute Reconciliation (Sample)
   For the agreed sample of business keys, every satellite attribute equals the SF Mirror source value. Pass criterion: 100% match on the agreed sample (status = PASS).

   Check ID: DM-A2
   Category: Attribute checks
   Sign-off criterion: Record-level attribute reconciliation (sample)
   Method: For each sampled (hash key, record source) unit, the current satellite
       row(s) are compared column by column with the source row(s) rebuilt from RAW using
       the model's own expressions (staging casts, derivations, unpivots, stitches, column
       maps)
   Pass criteria / tolerance: 100% match on agreed sample
   Owner: LUMIQ
   Vault location: BAGIC_PREPROD_CURATED_DB.BGIL_DATA_MODEL
   Maximus RAW: BAGIC_PROD_MIRROR_DB.MAXI_RAW
   Opus RAW (test): BAGIC_PREPROD_CURATED_DB.UTILS (prod:
       BAGIC_PROD_MIRROR_DB.OPUS_GG_DWHSTAGE)
   Scope: Every satellite model of maximus_partner_dv_dbt and opus_partner_dv_dbt
       (standard + augmented). Satellite tables are shared; rows are scoped by
       RECORD_SOURCE prefix (MAXIMUS / OPUS).
   Sample: 100 (hash key, RECORD_SOURCE) units per satellite, chosen deterministically
       by md5(hash key | record source | 'DM-A') so every re-run reads the same units.
       Change SAMPLE_SIZE in the generator to agree a different sample.
   Unit status: MATCH = exact; MATCH_DATE_FORMAT = equal once date/time text is
       normalised (type difference -- see DM-A1); SOURCE_CHANGED_AFTER_LOAD = source row
       newer than the last load (re-run after the next load, not a failure); NOT_IN_SOURCE
       = key no longer in RAW (see DM-K2, not a failure here); MISMATCH = fails
   Output columns: project, satellite, sampled_units, matched,
       matched_date_format_only, mismatched, source_changed_after_load, not_in_source,
       status, mismatch_examples (up to 20: hash key [record source] column: vault=... |
       source=...)

   GENERATED by validation/tools/gen_dm_a.py from the current dbt models -- edit the generator,
   not this file. The queries are IDENTICAL to those in the matching .docx.

   Revision notes:
   - Generated 2026-10-12 from the current opus_partner_dv_dbt and maximus_partner_dv_dbt
     models by validation/tools/gen_dm_a.py; results are blank and must be filled in
     after running the queries.
   - Scope: 98 MAXIMUS + 59 OPUS satellite models = 157 sections (141 single-active, 12
     multi-active, 4 object-column sats; 15 fed by an Opus stitch view).
   - Lineage is parsed, not typed: sat -> stg2 stage / wrapper / unpivot / stitch ->
     layer-1 stg_ -> RAW column. Hash keys reproduced as automate_dv 0.11.5 does:
     MD5_BINARY(NULLIF(UPPER(TRIM(CAST(<NK> AS VARCHAR))), '')).
   - Static finding: 58 satellite column(s) are loaded through an integer cast
     (try_to_number / ::number without scale); query (a) of DM-A1 reports DECIMALS LOST
     where the RAW column has a scale.
   - Lineage warnings (stage column excluded by src_column_map): 0.
   ===================================================================================== */


